{
  "name": "What to Expect During Your Bathroom Countertop Installation",
  "step": [
    {
      "name": "Step 1",
      "text": "Thinking about getting a new bathroom countertop? It's a pretty straightforward process, but knowing what's coming helps. First up, the old countertop needs to go, and any plumbing for the sink and faucet will be disconnected. Then, the vanity gets carefully measured and templated – this is super important for a perfect fit! After that, your new countertop will either be fabricated or cut to size. This can take a little time, usually about 10-15 business days from when they take the template until the final install. When it's ready, the team will set it in place, make sure it’s level, and seal it up nicely. Finally, the plumbing gets reconnected. Most standard countertop swaps can be done in about 1-3 days once the actual installation begins. You usually don't need a permit for a simple swap unless you're moving the sink or changing the plumbing around a lot. If you're looking for someone to handle all this smoothly in the greater Denver area, HH Remodeling can guide you through every step.",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 1
    }
  ],
